# Waveshare USB-TO-LoRa-HF candidate StratoPi configuration.
# Applied to the dongle selected by PORT in .env. Run on each host separately.
# Commands run from top to bottom. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
# These active setters CHANGE settings. Comment them out for inspection only.
# All lines are validated before opening the serial port.
# Firmware Ver1.2 supports the queries below. Each setter is followed by a
# readback that must match. The script pauses one second between commands.

# Enter command mode; AT+VER must follow immediately to confirm entry.
+++
AT+VER
AT+HELP

# Record current channel and spreading factor before changing settings.
AT+TXCH?
AT+RXCH?
AT+SF?

# 915 MHz, SF10, 500 kHz bandwidth, coding rate 4/5.
AT+TXCH=65
AT+TXCH?
AT+RXCH=65
AT+RXCH?
AT+SF=10
AT+SF?
AT+BW=2
AT+BW?
AT+CR=1
AT+CR?

# 10 dBm for initial nearby tests; shared stream-mode configuration.
AT+PWR=10
AT+PWR?
AT+MODE=1
AT+MODE?
AT+NETID=42
AT+NETID?
AT+ADDR=479
AT+ADDR?
AT+LBT=1
AT+LBT?
AT+RSSI=0
AT+RSSI?

# CRC is already enabled in the firmware; no CRC command is needed.
# Setters must return OK/+OK. Errors, timeouts, and echo-only AT replies fail.
# The +++ entry command may return only its echo; AT+VER confirms entry next.
# Save accepted changes and return to transparent mode.
AT+EXIT
